{"type": "mcq", "stem": "<p style=\"text-align: center;\"><math alttext=\"StartFraction RootIndex 3 StartRoot n Superscript 17 Baseline p Superscript 5 Baseline EndRoot Over 5 n squared left parenthesis RootIndex 8 StartRoot p Superscript 8 Baseline EndRoot right parenthesis EndFraction\"><mfrac><mroot><mrow><msup><mi>n</mi><mn>17</mn></msup><msup><mi>p</mi><mn>5</mn></msup></mrow><mn>3</mn></mroot><mrow><mn>5</mn><msup><mi>n</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mfenced><mroot><msup><mi>p</mi><mn>8</mn></msup><mn>8</mn></mroot></mfenced></mrow></mfrac></math></p>\n<p>For all positive values of <math alttext=\"n\"><mi>n</mi>\n</math> and <math alttext=\"p\"><mi>p</mi>\n</math>, the given expression is equivalent to which of the following?</p>\n<ol style=\"list-style-type: upper-roman;\">\n<li><math alttext=\"StartFraction left parenthesis n Superscript StartFraction 14 Over 3 EndFraction Baseline right parenthesis left parenthesis p Superscript five thirds Baseline right parenthesis Over 5 n p EndFraction\"><mfrac><mrow><mfenced><msup><mi>n</mi><mstyle displaystyle=\"true\"><mfrac><mn>14</mn><mn>3</mn></mfrac></mstyle></msup></mfenced><mfenced><msup><mi>p</mi><mstyle displaystyle=\"true\"><mfrac><mn>5</mn><mn>3</mn></mfrac></mstyle></msup></mfenced></mrow><mrow><mn>5</mn><mi>n</mi><mi>p</mi></mrow></mfrac></math><br /><br /></li>\n<li><math alttext=\"StartFraction RootIndex 3 StartRoot n Superscript 11 Baseline p squared EndRoot Over 5 EndFraction\"><mfrac><mroot><mrow><msup><mi>n</mi><mn>11</mn></msup><msup><mi>p</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mn>3</mn></mroot><mn>5</mn></mfrac></math></li>\n</ol>", "keys": ["78bb615b-1182-419f-840d-11a82877c87d"], "answerOptions": [{"id": "64e8b075-84b7-4546-bec1-1ebee8e5ed35", "content": "<p>I only</p>"}, {"id": "cae10e9f-77e6-4b98-968e-c58acf5ebcc2", "content": "<p>II only</p>"}, {"id": "78bb615b-1182-419f-840d-11a82877c87d", "content": "<p>I and II</p>"}, {"id": "53dda8cf-282c-422f-b845-b4e7fee8b517", "content": "<p>Neither I nor II</p>"}], "rationale": "<p>Choice C is correct. For positive values of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"a\"><mi>a</mi></math>, <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"RootIndex upper N StartRoot a EndRoot equals a Superscript StartFraction 1 Over upper N EndFraction\"><mroot><mi>a</mi><mi>N</mi></mroot><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>a</mi><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>N</mi></mfrac></msup></math>. Therefore, the given expression, <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"StartFraction RootIndex 3 StartRoot n Superscript 17 Baseline p Superscript 5 Baseline EndRoot Over 5 n squared left parenthesis RootIndex 8 StartRoot p Superscript 8 Baseline EndRoot right parenthesis EndFraction\"><mfrac><mroot><mrow><msup><mi>n</mi><mn>17</mn></msup><msup><mi>p</mi><mn>5</mn></msup></mrow><mn>3</mn></mroot><mrow><mn>5</mn><msup><mi>n</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mfenced><mroot><msup><mi>p</mi><mn>8</mn></msup><mn>8</mn></mroot></mfenced></mrow></mfrac></math>, can be rewritten as <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"StartFraction left parenthesis n Superscript 17 Baseline p Superscript 5 Baseline right parenthesis Superscript one third Baseline Over 5 n squared left parenthesis p Superscript 8 Baseline right parenthesis Superscript one eighth Baseline EndFraction\"><mfrac><msup><mfenced><mrow><msup><mi>n</mi><mn>17</mn></msup><msup><mi>p</mi><mn>5</mn></msup></mrow></mfenced><mstyle displaystyle=\"true\"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>3</mn></mfrac></mstyle></msup><mrow><mn>5</mn><msup><mi>n</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><msup><mfenced><msup><mi>p</mi><mn>8</mn></msup></mfenced><mstyle displaystyle=\"true\"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>8</mn></mfrac></mstyle></msup></mrow></mfrac></math>. Applying properties of exponents, this can be rewritten as <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"StartFraction n Superscript StartFraction 17 Over 3 EndFraction Baseline p Superscript five thirds Baseline Over 5 n squared p Superscript eight eighths Baseline EndFraction\"><mfrac><mrow><msup><mi>n</mi><mstyle displaystyle=\"true\"><mfrac><mn>17</mn><mn>3</mn></mfrac></mstyle></msup><msup><mi>p</mi><mstyle displaystyle=\"true\"><mfrac><mn>5</mn><mn>3</mn></mfrac></mstyle></msup></mrow><mrow><mn>5</mn><msup><mi>n</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><msup><mi>p</mi><mstyle displaystyle=\"true\"><mfrac><mn>8</mn><mn>8</mn></mfrac></mstyle></msup></mrow></mfrac></math>, or <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"StartFraction n Superscript StartFraction 17 Over 3 EndFraction Baseline p Superscript five thirds Baseline Over 5 n squared p EndFraction\"><mfrac><mrow><msup><mi>n</mi><mstyle displaystyle=\"true\"><mfrac><mn>17</mn><mn>3</mn></mfrac></mstyle></msup><msup><mi>p</mi><mstyle displaystyle=\"true\"><mfrac><mn>5</mn><mn>3</mn></mfrac></mstyle></msup></mrow><mrow><mn>5</mn><msup><mi>n</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mi>p</mi></mrow></mfrac></math>. Dividing the numerator and the denominator of this expression by <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"n\"><mi>n</mi></math> yields &nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"StartFraction n Superscript StartFraction 14 Over 3 EndFraction Baseline p Superscript five thirds Baseline Over 5 n p EndFraction\"><mfrac><mrow><msup><mi>n</mi><mstyle displaystyle=\"true\"><mfrac><mn>14</mn><mn>3</mn></mfrac></mstyle></msup><msup><mi>p</mi><mstyle displaystyle=\"true\"><mfrac><mn>5</mn><mn>3</mn></mfrac></mstyle></msup></mrow><mrow><mn>5</mn><mi>n</mi><mi>p</mi></mrow></mfrac></math>, which is statement I. Dividing the numerator and the denominator of this expression by <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"n p\"><mi>n</mi><mi>p</mi></math> yields <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"StartFraction n Superscript StartFraction 11 Over 3 EndFraction Baseline p Superscript two thirds Baseline Over 5 EndFraction\"><mfrac><mrow><msup><mi>n</mi><mstyle displaystyle=\"true\"><mfrac><mn>11</mn><mn>3</mn></mfrac></mstyle></msup><msup><mi>p</mi><mstyle displaystyle=\"true\"><mfrac><mn>2</mn><mn>3</mn></mfrac></mstyle></msup></mrow><mn>5</mn></mfrac></math>. This expression is equivalent to <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"StartFraction left parenthesis n Superscript 11 Baseline p squared right parenthesis Superscript one third Baseline Over 5 EndFraction\"><mfrac><msup><mfenced><mrow><msup><mi>n</mi><mn>11</mn></msup><msup><mi>p</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mfenced><mstyle displaystyle=\"true\"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>3</mn></mfrac></mstyle></msup><mn>5</mn></mfrac></math>. It follows that this expression is equivalent to <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"StartFraction RootIndex 3 StartRoot n Superscript 11 Baseline p squared EndRoot Over 5 EndFraction\"><mfrac><mroot><mrow><msup><mi>n</mi><mn>11</mn></msup><msup><mi>p</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mn>3</mn></mroot><mn>5</mn></mfrac></math>, which is statement II. Therefore, for all positive values of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"n\"><mi>n</mi></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"p\"><mi>p</mi></math>, the given expression is equivalent to I and II.</p>\n<p>Choice A is incorrect and may result from conceptual or calculation errors.</p>\n<p>Choice B is incorrect and may result from conceptual or calculation errors.</p>\n<p>Choice D is incorrect and may result from conceptual or calculation errors.</p>", "externalid": "8c278545-5668-4346-b11a-ea571647594f", "correct_answer": ["C"]}